TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum to control scope. Here's the breakdown:

---

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void SomeTest() { /* … */ }
}
```

---

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class (Class-Scoped Fixture)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void Test1() { }

    [Test]
    public void Test2() { }
}
```

> **Note:** `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods must be **static**.

---

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this assembly
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by attribute.

---

## 4. Once at the Very Start/End of the Entire Test Session

```csharp
public class TestSessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // runs once at the very start of the test run
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // runs once at the very end of the test run
    }
}
```

---

## Summary Table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|----------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes | `TestSessionContext` |

All hooks support `async Task` return types if you need async setup/teardown. The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) come from `TUnit.Core`.
